  "important": "Important",
  "medicalWarning": "OctoSense is not a medical device and does not diagnose conditions.",
  "topic1Title": "Vital signs and context",
  "topic1P1": "The body continuously produces signals such as heart rate, movement, sleep, and energy expenditure.",
  "topic1P2": "A single number represents only one moment and needs context to be understood.",
  "topic1P3": "Looking at changes over time can reveal natural patterns in the body.",
  "topic1P4": "OctoSense organizes these readings to make them easier to understand and does not turn a reading into a diagnosis.",
  "topic2Title": "Heart rate",
  "topic2P1": "The heart pumps blood to distribute oxygen and nutrients throughout the body.",
  "topic2P2": "Heart rate can change with exercise, rest, emotions, temperature, and other factors.",
  "topic2P3": "Watches estimate heart rate from signals captured at the skin.",
  "topic2P4": "Comparing different periods and situations helps explain why the number changes.",
  "topic3Title": "Sleep and recovery",
  "topic3P1": "During sleep, the body cycles through different stages with important roles in recovery.",
  "topic3P2": "Wearables use movement and other signals to estimate sleep periods.",
  "topic3P3": "These estimates do not replace specialized sleep testing.",
  "topic3P4": "Regularity, duration, and context are more informative than a single night.",
  "topic4Title": "Steps and movement",
  "topic4P1": "Step count is a simple way to represent movement throughout the day.",
  "topic4P2": "Accelerometers detect changes in motion across multiple axes.",
  "topic4P3": "Algorithms filter these signals to estimate events consistent with steps.",
  "topic4P4": "The result is an estimate and can vary with the device and walking pattern.",
  "topic5Title": "PPG and light",
  "topic5P1": "PPG stands for photoplethysmography and uses light to observe blood-volume changes near the skin.",
  "topic5P2": "LEDs illuminate the skin while a sensor measures reflected or received light.",
  "topic5P3": "The light pattern changes with each heartbeat and can be processed to estimate heart rate.",
  "topic5P4": "Motion, strap fit, and skin characteristics can affect the signal.",
  "topic6Title": "Accelerometer",
  "topic6P1": "An accelerometer measures acceleration across different axes.",
  "topic6P2": "In a watch, it can detect changes associated with steps, gestures, and periods of movement.",
  "topic6P3": "The sensor does not know what a person is doing by itself: algorithms interpret the patterns.",
  "topic6P4": "Different activities can produce similar signals and may require additional context.",
  "topic7Title": "Oxygen saturation and SpO₂",
  "topic7P1": "Peripheral oxygen saturation, known as SpO₂, estimates the proportion of hemoglobin bound to oxygen.",
  "topic7P2": "Optical sensors use differences in light absorption to estimate that proportion.",
  "topic7P3": "The result depends on signal quality and measurement conditions.",
  "topic7P4": "A wearable reading should be understood as an estimate, not a clinical diagnosis.",
  "topic8Title": "Hemoglobin and oxygen",
  "topic8P1": "Hemoglobin is a protein found in red blood cells.",
  "topic8P2": "It can bind reversibly to oxygen and transport it through the body.",
  "topic8P3": "The relationship Hb + O₂ ⇌ HbO₂ represents this reversible transport.",
  "topic8P4": "This process connects chemistry, biology, and physiology in one phenomenon.",
  "topic9Title": "Energy and metabolism",
  "topic9P1": "Cells need energy continuously to maintain their functions.",
  "topic9P2": "Metabolism includes chemical reactions that transform nutrients and support cellular processes.",
  "topic9P3": "During physical activity, energy demand increases and the body adjusts several systems.",
  "topic9P4": "Wearables can estimate energy expenditure using signals and models, but they do not directly measure every metabolic reaction.",
  "topic10Title": "Cardiovascular system",
  "topic10P1": "The cardiovascular system integrates the heart, blood, and blood vessels.",
  "topic10P2": "It distributes oxygen, nutrients, hormones, and heat while removing metabolic products.",
  "topic10P3": "Exercise increases muscle demand and triggers coordinated cardiovascular responses.",
  "topic10P4": "Heart-rate data can help visualize part of this process in accessible language.",
  "topic11Title": "From sensor to data",
  "topic11P1": "The path begins with a physical sensor that turns a body phenomenon into an electrical or optical signal.",
  "topic11P2": "The device processes that signal and applies algorithms to estimate a metric.",
  "topic11P3": "A platform such as Health Connect can organize and share authorized data with apps.",
  "topic11P4": "OctoSense turns these metrics into clear visualizations and explanations.",
  "topic12Title": "How to interpret trends",
  "topic12P1": "A trend looks at changes across a period rather than drawing a conclusion from one value.",
  "topic12P2": "Averages, totals, and time series reduce the focus on a single measurement.",
  "topic12P3": "It is also important to consider incomplete days, routine changes, and device differences.",
  "topic12P4": "Good interpretation combines data, context, and measurement limits.",
